    "pages": [
      {
        "id": "p0",
        "title": "The Knockdown Is Half the Reward",
        "text": "After a knockdown the opponent HAS to stand up into whatever you prepared - that is okizeme. A meaty attack timed onto their first vulnerable frame beats almost everything they can press."
      },
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "title": "Meaty or Bait - Read Them",
        "text": "A nervous opponent with meter may press a reversal on wakeup. Bait it, block, and let it finish; once you recognize its recovery, that is where a punish belongs. Against a passive opponent, take the free meaty pressure instead."
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "title": "The Drill",
        "text": "Finish the knockdown route, then practice three answers: a meaty timed onto the rise, a delayed throw against a guarding wakeup, and the patient bait that safely waits out a reversal."
      }
    ],
